Appendix A: Structure-Disruption-Stabilization (S-D-S) Pedagogical Protocol
The Structure-Disruption-Stabilization (S-D-S) pedagogical model was administered to the Experimental Group (EG) over a 24-week intervention period comprising 72 sessions (3 sessions/week, 90 minutes/session; 108 cumulative instructional hours). The protocol aims to systematically dismantle L1-mediated translation loops and establish direct concept-to-L2 mappings.
       Phase 1: Structure (W1–W8)
  [Visual/Spatial Concept] ──(Direct Mapping)──> [L2 Lemma & Syntax]
               │ (Strict No-Gloss Policy)
               ▼
       Phase 2: Disruption (W9–W16)
  [L1 Competitor Node] ──(Speeded Inhibition / High-Pressure Tasks)──X (Suppressed)
               │ (Rapid Semantic Stroop & Paraphrase)
               ▼
      Phase 3: Stabilization (W17–W24)
  [Multi-modal Concept Core] ════(Automatized Direct Access)════> [Fluent L2 Output]
