Appendix B: Technical EEG Specifications, Preprocessing Pipeline, and ICA Rejection
Electroencephalographic (EEG) recordings were acquired longitudinally across three experimental waves: Baseline (Month 1), Mid-Intervention (Month 3), and Post-Intervention (Month 6).
1. Acquisition Hardware & Electrode Array
	System: 64-channel BioSemi ActiveTwo active-electrode system.
	Electrode Placement: Extended International 10–20 layout mounted in an elastic cap.
	Reference & Ground: Common Mode Sense (CMS) active electrode and Driven Right Leg (DRL) passive electrode forming a feedback loop.
	Sampling Rate: 500" Hz" online acquisition (24"-bit"  A/D resolution).
	Impedances: Maintained strictly below 10" k" Ω(offset voltage <±20" mV" ) across all channels prior to recording.
	EOG Configuration: 4 electrooculographic channels (bipolar vertical VEOG above/below the left eye for blinks; bipolar horizontal HEOG at the outer canthi of both eyes for saccades).
2. Preprocessing Pipeline (EEGLAB / MATLAB)
	Re-Referencing: Raw continuous signals were re-referenced offline to the mathematically computed algebraic average of the left and right mastoids (("M1" +"M2" )/2).
	Bandpass Filtering: A zero-phase Hamming windowed sinc FIR filter (EEGLAB pop_eegfiltnew) was applied: 
	High-pass cutoff: 0.1" Hz" (6" dB/octave"  rolloff, transition bandwidth 0.2" Hz" ).
	Low-pass cutoff: 30" Hz" (24" dB/octave"  rolloff, transition bandwidth 7.5" Hz" ).
	Notch filter: 50" Hz" infinite impulse response (IIR) notch filter to eliminate power-line interference.
	Epoching & Baseline Correction: Continuous data were segmented into stimulus-locked epochs spanning from -200" ms" pre-stimulus to +800" ms" post-stimulus onset. Epochs were baseline-corrected relative to the -200" ms" to 0" ms" pre-stimulus mean amplitude.
	Independent Component Analysis (ICA): Extended Infomax ICA (Bell & Sejnowski, 1995) was performed on un-epoched, filtered continuous datasets. Independent components (ICs) representing blink artifacts, horizontal saccadic deflections, and high-frequency temporalis myogenic bursts were identified and subtracted using spatial topographies, frequency spectra, and time-course activity profiles via ICLabel (Pion-Tonachini et al., 2019).
	Artifact Rejection: Post-ICA epochs containing residual amplitudes exceeding ±75" " μ"V" , voltage steps >50" " μ"V"/"ms" , or flatline segments >100" ms" were flagged and automatically rejected. Across all cohorts and timepoints, an average of 94.3%of trials were retained for grand averaging.
                                            
Raw 64-Ch Continuous EEG (500 Hz)
  │
  ├──> Re-reference to Mastoid Average [(M1+M2)/2]
  ├──> Bandpass Filter [0.1 – 30 Hz FIR] + 50 Hz Notch
  ├──> Extended Infomax ICA ──> Subtraction of Blink / Saccade / Myogenic ICs
  ├──> Epoch Segmentation [-200 ms to +800 ms]
  ├──> Baseline Correction [-200 ms to 0 ms]
  └──> Residual Artifact Threshold Rejection (±75 μV)
        │
        └──> Grand-Averaged ERP Waveforms (N400 Window: 300–500 ms)
             Target ROI: Centro-Parietal (Cz, CP1, CP2, Pz)
