Appendix C: Full Statistical Model Formulations & Syntax
Statistical analyses were executed in the R computational environment (v4.3.2) utilizing the geepack and lme4 packages.
1. Generalized Estimating Equations (GEE) for Overdispersed Longitudinal Count Data
For discrete non-negative integer counts exhibiting longitudinal within-subject clustering (L1_Req and L1_Calque), Generalized Estimating Equations with a Poisson error distribution, a logarithmic link function, and a first-order autoregressive correlation structure ("AR" (1)) were fitted:
log⁡(μ_ij )=β_0+β_1 (〖"Group" 〗_i )+β_2 (〖"Month" 〗_ij )+β_3 (〖"Group" 〗_i×〖"Month" 〗_ij )

"Var" (Y_ij )=ϕ⋅μ_ij

where idenotes the individual participant (i=1,…,40) and jdenotes the longitudinal wave (j∈{1ⓜ,3ⓜ,6}). Standard errors were estimated using the robust Huber-White sandwich estimator.
R Syntax (geepack):
