Appendix D: Rubric for the Evaluation of Direct Conceptual Fluency (1–10 Scale)
The Conceptual Fluency Scale assesses real-time oral production on a 10-point continuum, focusing on the reduction of L1 mediation, processing delays, and syntactic calquing.
[Score 1–3: Low]        ──> Heavy L1 mediation; frequent silent/filled pauses; literal calquing.
[Score 4–6: Moderate]   ──> Emerging automatization; occasional L1 intrusions; circumlocution.
[Score 7–10: High]      ──> Direct concept-to-form access; native-like cadence; zero translation pauses.
